weeks after Aaron's arrival at Northstar. Hypothermia, stress, and malnutrition would have all caused the ulcer to worsen. Aaron had been complaining of stomach pain since almost the beginning of his time at Northstar. If the ulcer had been diagnosed early on, it could have been cured by an over-the-counter medication. If Aaron had been taken to hospital as late as the day before his death or even hours before his final collapse, his life would most likely have been saved by antibiotics and proper medical care. A few days after the Bacon's viewed their son's body, they received a call at home from a television reporter who was also based in

