accounts, such as how Aaron was punished by having food withheld. During interviews, the other teenagers in Aaron's group said that sometimes they'd tried to help him by sneaking in food and sharing their blankets, but usually they were too scared to do so due to the punishments that would follow if caught. Deputy Bernards cross-checked the campers' claims against provable data, such as what the temperature and weather conditions were during Arren's month at Northstar. She calculated that Arren had been forced to sleep 14 nights in the desert without a sleeping bag. For four of these nights, he didn't even have a blanket. He had been deprived of food entirely for a total of 11 days. These punishments were in direct violation of Northstar's own code

