We didn't break them down to punish them. We broke them down to get rid of the old crap and help them be a better and more positive person. Some of the kids were so scared they'd almost pass out. And that was fine by me. I wanted them to have a little fear." Aaron Bacon's parents still feel that the adults involved in their son's death paid too small a price for their role in his demise. They have spoken out against Lance Jagger's assertion that he's providing tough love, with Sally Bacon telling ABC News, "...you can do tough love as a parent because you love the child. They can do tough. They can't do love." Police gave Sally and Bob their son's journal after they had copied its contents as evidence.

